# Shell scripts run under sh/bash on every host - CI (Linux, macOS), WSL, git-bash - so their working-tree line
# endings are LF whatever core.autocrlf says. Without this a Windows checkout hands WSL a script whose `set -eu`
# is `set -eu\r`, which dash rejects with "Illegal option -". The macOS zip's "Self-sign (optional).command" is
# the same script under another name.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.command text eol=lf
